      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test file and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It creates a `BritishCutoverChronology` instance and verifies that year `1000005` (a post-cutover year not divisible by 4) is not a leap year. Let me write an improved version with better understandability.Now let me compile-check the test.The improved test compiled successfully (`COMPILE_OK`). The refactored test improves understandability by removing unused imports, renaming `boolean0` to `isLeap` and the magic literal to `postCutoverYearNotDivisibleByFour`, and adding a Javadoc comment explaining why year 1000005 is not a leap year under the British Cutover chronology's Gregorian rules."
